/E (At the same time, they state that the concept of reliability, despite the difficulties of deriving it under non-stationary conditions, is still, as in stationary conditions, a better practical tool. This is because it accounts for the variability of conditions \(non-stationarity\) and provides answers regarding safety within the assumed planning horizon.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [18]
>>
